<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::policy_rate_expect" target="global_market_turbulence::global_bond_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">If markets revise up expected central-bank policy paths due to conflict-driven inflation or supply shocks, sovereign and high-grade yields reprices upward across markets to reflect tighter future monetary policy.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_turbulence</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::policy_rate_expect" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::election_policy_bias" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Russia-Ukraine shocks lift inflation and push market expectations toward tighter central-bank paths, constraining fiscal room and encouraging governments to adopt short-term, visible tech trade/tax measures timed for elections.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::policy_rate_expect" target="us_iran_standoff::rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">War-driven commodity and risk shocks prompt reassessments of central-bank tightening, pushing up market-implied short- and medium-term policy-rate paths that feed into rate expectations relevant to US policy posture in the Iran standoff.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
