<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::tech_invest_momentum" target="global_market_turbulence::tech_equity_valuation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A geopolitically induced pullback in venture and corporate capex into AI/semiconductor projects reduces projected growth and funding, which compresses forward earnings assumptions and technology sector valuation multiples over the medium term.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_turbulence</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::tech_invest_momentum" target="state_crypto_cybercrime::cyberattack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained rises in tech and cyber defense investment driven by the conflict fund improved detection, patching and response capabilities, which over the medium term reduce the incidence of successful intrusions.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">state_crypto_cybercrime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::tech_invest_momentum" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::energy_infra_security" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained war-driven increases in defense- and resilience-oriented tech funding accelerate deployment of cybersecurity, grid hardening and redundant power capacity for data centers and fabs, improving energy infrastructure security relevant to the US–China tech competition.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
