<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="global_market_turbulence::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened cross-asset price swings from wartime news prompt institutional de-risking (stop-losses, reduced leverage) and retail flight from risky positions, directly lowering aggregate willingness to accept risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_turbulence</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="state_crypto_cybercrime::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute increases in market volatility from war shocks trigger margin calls, mark-to-market losses and heightened uncertainty, prompting investors to shift allocations into safer assets and lower overall risk-taking.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">state_crypto_cybercrime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">War-driven spikes in commodity and geopolitical risk premia trigger re-pricing and cross-border capital flows that amplify price swings specifically in equities, FX and bonds tied to the US–China tech sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="us_iran_standoff::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Volatility spikes originating from the Russia–Ukraine war transmit across asset classes and time zones via correlated selling, cross-hedging and volatility trading, producing near-term increases in market volatility metrics during episodes of US–Iran friction.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
