<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_supply_risk" target="global_market_turbulence::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.92</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher assessed probability of physical disruption to oil/gas raises immediate spot and futures bids as market participants price in a supply shortfall and risk premia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_turbulence</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_supply_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::oil_supply_demand_gap" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened risk to oil production and shipping from a US–Iran standoff (e.g., attacks, insurance/shipping reroutes, temporary shutdowns) directly reduces available supply into global markets, widening the supply–demand gap that also affects energy conditions around the Russia–Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_supply_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::policy_rate_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute oil‑supply risk raises oil prices and near‑term inflation pressure in European and global markets, which in turn pushes up market expectations for tighter central‑bank policy relevant to countries engaged with the Russia–Ukraine war.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_supply_risk" target="state_crypto_cybercrime::commodity_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher risk of physical disruptions to oil and gas supply from the Gulf sharply raises energy price uncertainty and triggers larger, more frequent swings in energy markets that spill over into broader commodity pricing.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">state_crypto_cybercrime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_supply_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in assessed probability/severity of Persian Gulf supply disruptions causes traders and refiners to bid up futures and spot crude prices immediately to pre-price potential shortfalls and risk premia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_supply_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::energy_infra_security" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher risk of supply disruption in the Iran standoff translates into more frequent or higher-severity incidents (attacks, seizures, or denials of service) that directly degrade the operational integrity and availability of pipelines, terminals and shipping in affected corridors.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
