<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension" target="global_market_turbulence::global_bond_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalations in geopolitical tension around tech supply chains and sanctions drive safe-haven flows into core sovereign debt (e.g., U.S. Treasuries, bunds), putting downward pressure on average high-grade global bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_turbulence</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension" target="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in geopolitical tension driven by intensifying US–China tech rivalry prompts rapid global portfolio rebalancing and hedging (risk‑off flows, flight to cash, option buying) that directly raises realized and implied volatility in markets tied to the Russia–Ukraine conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension" target="russia_ukraine_war::oil_supply_demand_gap" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased geopolitical tension related to the US–China tech dispute raises the probability of sanctions, shipping interruptions or targeted attacks on energy logistics, producing near‑term crude flow disruptions and inventory draws that widen the oil supply–demand gap.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension" target="state_crypto_cybercrime::cyberattack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising geopolitical tensions prompt states to authorize more offensive cyber operations and to outsource or tacitly tolerate criminal cyber actors targeting adversary networks, increasing successful cyber intrusions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">state_crypto_cybercrime</data>
