  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Degradation of energy-infrastructure security (including cyberattacks on pipelines, terminals, or refineries plausibly linked to tech-conflict operations) causes supply interruptions and logistics bottlenecks that raise global crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_turbulence</data>
